# BMP581 barometric path — decoded defmt excerpts (2026-07-19)
#
# First sim pass with a barometer: sim/NRF52840_TWIM.cs (a real TWIM master —
# the stock twi1 models the legacy byte interface embassy-nrf never programs)
# + sim/BMP581.cs (the sensor, with a scripted altitude source). Every run
# below is `bin/watch-sim.sh --phone-port 7797`, DEFMT_LOG=debug, driven from
# one long-lived monitor connection.

## The task comes alive — it used to park on a timed-out probe
0.000671 INFO  baro: BMP581 streaming
# (was: "baro: no BMP581 on I2C (probe timed out); task parked")

## Scripted altitude round-trips through pressure and back to the firmware
# monitor: sysbus.twi1.bmp581 SetAltitudeMeters 1600   (the model's default)
1.000671 DEBUG baro: alt=1599.9999m gain=0.0m loss=0.0m
# 0.1 mm of round-trip error: the model inverts the same ISA constants
# watch_core::elevation::altitude_m applies.

## GPS-baro complementary filter engages (bench_jog, GGA alt 1624.0)
# Pure baro-only for the first SEED_SAMPLES pairings, then the seed lands and
# the published altitude re-frames onto the weather-unbiased GPS altitude —
# the auto-QNH correction, observed end to end for the first time.
38.000671 DEBUG baro: alt=1599.9999m gain=0.0m loss=0.0m
39.000671 DEBUG baro: alt=1624.18m    gain=0.0m loss=0.0m
40.000671 DEBUG baro: alt=1624.1823m  gain=0.0m loss=0.0m

## VERT accrues over a scripted climb + descent (mountain_loop)
# monitor: sysbus.twi1.bmp581 StartTriangleProfile 1600 1800 417 660
#   (417/660 mm/s track the fixture's own GPS altitude ramp, so baro and GPS
#    co-vary and the complementary filter is exercised, not bypassed)
18:16:29 [INFO] twi1.bmp581: triangle profile 1600..1800 m, +417/-660 mm/s
169.000793 DEBUG baro: alt=1651.0803m gain=51.83484m  loss=0.0m
527.000793 DEBUG baro: alt=1708.2245m gain=133.8728m  loss=20.082764m

### Run dashboard at t=530 s (frame-dump transcription)
#   0:08:50                                    PAU
#   [foot] 0.49 KM                             D+E
#   PACE 18:04 /KM
#   NOW  8:46 /KM
#   [heart] --
#   [mtn]  1704 M            <- ALT prefers the barometric reading
#   [vert] +133 -23 M        <- VERT gain/loss, both accruing
#   [sat]  9 SATS PERF

## The ALT row really is the barometer, not fix.alt_m
# Set a static altitude far from the fixture's GPS altitude (~1700 m) and the
# row follows the barometer within one sample:
# monitor: sysbus.twi1.bmp581 SetAltitudeMeters 2400
559.000701 DEBUG baro: alt=2306.2747m gain=766.975m loss=57.32129m
#   [mtn]  2324 M
#   [vert] +766 -39 M
# (2324, not 2400: the complementary bias — baro minus GPS — is subtracted,
#  which is the auto-QNH correction doing its job. It then slews back.)

## Elevation mini-profile sparkline, baro-driven (ElevationProfile page)
# BTN3 x18 from the Dashboard. Transcription at t=190 s:
#   ELEV D+61 D-0
#   <sparkline: a monotonic climb across the full 168 px panel width>
#   GPS  10 SATS PERF

## Manual QNH re-zero — both previously bench-gated paths
### SET <alt>: idle face, fresh fix (gps_dropout, GGA alt 1624.0)
12.176879 INFO  button: BTN3 long -> qnh re-zero requested
12.176879 INFO  baro: qnh re-zero -> Applied(1624.0)
# Frame: 2x banner "SET 1624M" over the idle face, and the ALT row below it
# reads 1624 M — the bias snap is visible in the published altitude, not just
# the banner (the raw barometer is still at 1600 m).
#   SET 1624M
#   GPS  8 SATS
#   LAT     40.01500
#   LON  -105.27018
#   SPD  3.0 M/S
#   ALT  1624 M
#   VERT +0 -0 M

### NO GPS FIX: the same press inside the fixture's 40 s void window
87.344116 INFO  button: BTN3 long -> qnh re-zero requested
87.344177 INFO  baro: qnh re-zero -> NoGps
#   NO GPS FIX
#   GPS  STALE 10S
#   ...
#   ALT  1624 M            <- unchanged: a refusal is a no-op, not a snap
# (The NO BARO variant was already verified on 2026-07-19 with the task parked.)

## Phantom-vert moving gate, both directions
